---
description: Never break iOS Home Screen top/bottom safe-area chrome when changing theme, headers, or layout.
alwaysApply: true
---

# iOS PWA safe-area chrome (do not regress)

KinSight is an iOS Home Screen PWA with `viewport-fit: cover` and
`apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style: black-translucent`. The webview
draws **under** the clock. The native bar does **not** also offset the
webview. Getting this wrong is why headers jump: too much inset (empty
band under the clock) or too little (title hidden behind the clock).

## Locked layout

- **Viewport:** `html, body { height: 100%; overflow: hidden }`. `body` is `position: relative` and **not** a flex column. Do **not** `overflow-y: auto` on `body` — that breaks iOS `position: fixed` on the tab bar. Page content scrolls in `main.app-scroll`. The nav is a viewport-fixed body child.
- **Top (once):** `pt-[env(safe-area-inset-top)]` on `PageShell` only. Do not also put it on `#app-root`, `main`, or `PageHeader`.
- **Bottom nav:** locked in `.cursor/rules/bottom-navigation.mdc`. Do not restyle `BottomNav` from page or theme work.
- Status-bar **paint** (`.theme-status-fill`, `.app-shell::before`) may use the same `env(safe-area-inset-top, 0px)` height. They are `position: fixed` and must not add a second layout gap.

## Never

- A 59px (or any) **minimum** on top inset (`max(env(...), 59px)`).
- JS that sets `--app-sat` / padding-top to `0px` to “fix” a tall header.
- Extra `env(safe-area-inset-top)` on `PageHeader`, page roots, or Home **in addition** to `main.app-scroll`.
- Switching status-bar-style to `default` and keeping app-shell top padding (double bar).
- Removing app-shell top padding while leaving `black-translucent` (title under the clock).
- Using theme toggles as an excuse to change these insets.

## If a screenshot looks wrong

- Empty band under the clock → something **stacked** a second top inset. Remove the extra one; do not delete the app-shell inset.
- Title/search in the status bar → app-shell top inset is missing. Restore it. Do not invent a heuristic.

Theme work only changes **colors** (`theme-color`, html/body background, fill color). It does not change inset math.
